    "text": "<p>Given below is the plot of a potential energy function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> for a system, in which a particle is in one dimensional motion, while a conservative force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> acts on it. Suppose that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mtext>mech&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>, the incorrect statement for this system is :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f7dd0df4-adcb-4dcd-81ed-0b0628b65d9b-image.png\" style=\"width: 284px; height: 242px;\" /></p>",
